Z||000005||Blacktree||12-20-2001||01:19 AM||||Depending on which body panel you're referring to, it could be:<P>1) sheet-molded compound (i.e. SMC), which is basically glass fiber impregnated with plastic (hood, roof, rear clip, decklid, etc)... which is also called FRP (fiberglass reinforced plastic)<P>2) injection-molded urethane (front and rear fasciae, door skins, rocker panels, etc)<P>3) phenolic resin (front and rear quarter-panels, some other parts that I can't think of right now)<P>I don't know the trade names of the various compounds, though.<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.tweaktech.com" TARGET=_blank>Tweaktech</A><p>[This message has been edited by Blacktree (edited 12-20-2001).]||||reg||1
